@startuml us120_domain_model_excerpt
title Team Domain Model — Excerpt Relevant to US120 (Flight DSL Semantic Validation)
caption Subset extracted from the team's conceptual Domain Model\n(docs/sprint-3/domain-model/domain-model.puml).\n\nThis excerpt is the *target* model that the Flight DSL describes —\nthe US120 semantic validator does **not** load these aggregates from\npersistence; it operates on the AST (see class diagram) whose nodes\nmirror the concepts shown here one-to-one. Implementation status of\neach class is independent of US120.

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classBackgroundColor #D6EAF8
skinparam classBorderColor      #5B9BD5
skinparam packageStyle           rectangle
skinparam packageBorderColor     #888888
skinparam defaultFontSize        11
hide empty members
left to right direction

' ============================================================
' Flight Aggregate — the semantic validator reads and validates
' the AST representation of this aggregate's structure.
' ============================================================
package "Flight Aggregate" {
    class Flight <<aggregate root>>
    class FlightDesignator <<value object>>
    abstract class Departure <<value object>>
    class CharterDeparture <<value object>>
    class RegularDeparture <<value object>>

    class FlightPlan <<entity>> {
        flightPlanID
    }
    class FlightLeg <<entity>>
    class DepartureInfo <<value object>>
    class ArrivalInfo <<value object>>
    class FuelLoad <<value object>>
    class FlightSegment <<entity>>
    class Waypoint <<value object>>
    class Coordinates <<value object>>
    class AltitudeSlot <<value object>>
    class WindDirection <<value object>>
    class WindSpeed <<value object>>
    enum FlightPlanStatus <<enum>> {
        DRAFT
        VALIDATED
        TESTED
    }

    CharterDeparture --|> Departure
    RegularDeparture --|> Departure

    Flight *-- FlightDesignator
    Flight *-- Departure
    Flight *-- "1..*" FlightPlan

    FlightPlan *-- FlightPlanStatus
    FlightPlan *-- "1..*" FlightLeg

    FlightLeg *-- DepartureInfo
    FlightLeg *-- ArrivalInfo
    FlightLeg *-- FuelLoad
    FlightLeg *-- "1..*" FlightSegment

    FlightSegment *-- "2" Waypoint : start, end
    FlightSegment *-- "1..*" AltitudeSlot
    FlightSegment *-- WindDirection
    FlightSegment *-- WindSpeed

    Waypoint *-- Coordinates
}

' ============================================================
' Airport Aggregate — referenced by departures/arrivals
' ============================================================
package "Airport Aggregate" {
    class Airport <<aggregate root>>
    class AirportIATACode <<value object>>
    class AirportICAOCode <<value object>>

    Airport *-- AirportIATACode
    Airport *-- AirportICAOCode
}

' ============================================================
' FlightRoute Aggregate — validated at flight level
' ============================================================
package "FlightRoute Aggregate" {
    class FlightRoute <<aggregate root>>
    class RouteName <<value object>>

    FlightRoute *-- RouteName
}

' ============================================================
' Cross-aggregate references used by the semantic rules
' ============================================================
Flight         --> FlightRoute     : for route
DepartureInfo  --> Airport         : from
ArrivalInfo    --> Airport         : to
FlightRoute    --> "2" Airport     : origin, destination

' ============================================================
' Mapping note for US120 semantic rules
' ============================================================
note as MappingNote
  **What the semantic validator checks against the domain**

  **Flight-level rules (FlightLevelRule)**
   • FlightDesignator must be unique → S: FLIGHT_ID_NOT_UNIQUE
   • Flight type must be REGULAR or CHARTER → S: FLIGHT_TYPE_INVALID

  **Leg-level rules (LegLevelRule)**
   • Each FlightPlan has ≥1 FlightLeg → S: FLIGHT_MISSING_LEGS
   • Each FlightLeg has DepartureInfo/ArrivalInfo/FuelLoad/Segments
   • FuelLoad quantity > 0 → S: FUEL_NOT_POSITIVE

  **Leg-sequence rules (LegSequenceRule)**
   • ArrivalInfo airport of leg n = DepartureInfo airport of leg n+1
     → S: LEG_SEQUENCE_AIRPORT_MISMATCH
   • Arrival time of leg n < departure time of leg n+1
     → S: LEG_SEQUENCE_TIME_NOT_ORDERED

  **Route-coherence rules (RouteCoherenceRule)**
   • FlightRoute origin = first-leg departure airport
     → S: ROUTE_ORIGIN_MISMATCH
   • FlightRoute destination = last-leg arrival airport
     → S: ROUTE_DESTINATION_MISMATCH
   • No airport visited twice → S: ROUTE_AIRPORT_REPEATED

  **Segment-coherence rules (SegmentCoherenceRule)**
   • Waypoint start ≠ Waypoint end → S: SEGMENT_START_EQUALS_END

  **Domain-consistency rules (DomainConsistencyRule)**
   • AirportIATACode/AirportICAOCode format → S: AIRPORT_CODE_BAD_FORMAT
   • AltitudeSlot/WindSpeed positive → S: NUMERIC_NOT_POSITIVE
   • DepartureInfo/ArrivalInfo datetime valid → S: DATETIME_INVALID_CALENDAR
end note

MappingNote .. FlightPlan
@enduml